<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarsa Dengel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1550–<a href="/years/1597">1597</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarsa Dengel was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in the second half of the sixteenth century. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> profile, he defeated and executed the Adal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-v-of-adal">Sultan Muhammad V</a> in 1577. This defeat, together with others, permanently ended the Adal Sultanate as a military power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarsa-dengel.jpg" alt="Sarsa Dengel" width="302" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ZemenfesKidus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Western_kings_on_Horseback_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
